{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception (obstacle sensors) and motion capabilities (discrete actions). The specification automata enforce safe, efficient exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot recovery turns. Full_rotate is reserved for rare, deliberate scans. The supervisor never allows forward or random_walk actions when an obstacle is detected in front, and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensors) and motion (actions)",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and strong exploration bias"
  ],
